isions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned."},"laws":[],"number":"1180","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Economics and Public Finance","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"C001116","district":9,"fullName":"Rep. Clyde, Andrew S. [R-GA-9]","party":"R","state":"GA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-02-11","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p>This bill repeals the Impoundment Control Act of 1974 (ICA).&nbsp;The&nbsp;ICA generally limits the authority of the President to impound (i.e., withhold from obligation or expenditure) funds that have been appropriated by Congress and establishes related procedures. It&nbsp;also establishes expedited legislative procedures that Congress may use to consider legislation to enact rescissions proposed by the President.&nbsp;</p>","updateDate":"2025-09-26T15:22:53Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"To repeal the Impoundment Control Act of 1974.","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-08T19:31:27Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-08T19:31:27Z"}
